---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="XDIRGA BLOG privacy policy: this blog collects no personal data, has no third-party trackers, and only your theme preference is stored in your browser."
  lang="en"
  hreflang={{ en: new URL('/en/privacy/', SITE.url).href, id: new URL('/privasi/', SITE.url).href }}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] pt-10 sm:pt-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[2.3rem] leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-text sm:text-[2.9rem]">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-text-secondary">Last updated 15 November 2026.</p>
    <div class="prose mt-8 max-w-none">
      <h2>Data collected</h2>
      <p>
        This blog does not collect personal data. There is no sign-up form, no comments, no third-party trackers, and no ads that monitor readers.
      </p>
      <h2>Browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        The only thing stored in your browser is your theme preference: light, dark, or follow the system. That value lives in your own browser's local storage, is never sent to the server, and can be deleted at any time through your browser settings.
      </p>
      <h2>Outbound links</h2>
      <p>
        Some articles link to other sites as sources. Those sites have their own privacy policies, outside this blog's control.
      </p>
      <h2>Ads and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This blog shows ads from Google AdSense. Ads only load after you accept through the consent banner that appears on your first visit. If you decline, no ads and no ad scripts load at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google may use cookies to show personalized ads, for example based on the topics you read. Your banner choice is stored in your own browser's local storage, is never sent to the server, and can be changed at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can turn off ad personalization at any time through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google Ad Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices">aboutads.info</a>. This blog does not sell reader data to any third party.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the update date above changes with it. Meaningful changes will be noted on this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
